# Example external profile that includes SAST-SEMGREP-064.
#
# How to use:
#   1) Run: oss-policy-kit scan-sast --target .
#      This produces .oss-policy-kit/evidence/sast-semgrep.json. When Semgrep
#      is not installed locally, the evidence file is still written with
#      status: not_available; SAST-SEMGREP-064 will then report
#      manual-review-required (honest gap, not a crash).
#   2) Copy this file into your repository (or anywhere on disk) and edit it.
#   3) Run: oss-policy-kit evaluate --target . --profile ./external-with-sast.yaml
#
# This file is NOT a bundled profile. It exists as a starting template.
# Edit `controls:` freely. External profiles cannot override built-in evaluators.
# See docs/cli-reference.md and src/oss_policy_kit/data/profiles/github-level-2/profile.yaml
# for the bundled controls you may want to copy here.

id: external-with-sast
title: External profile combining github-level-2 with Semgrep SAST evidence
description: >
  External profile example that augments a typical clone-side baseline with
  SAST-SEMGREP-064 evidence-backed coverage. Run scan-sast before evaluate
  so the evidence file exists; missing or `not_available` evidence will
  surface as manual-review-required by design.
audience: Teams that want SAST evidence as part of their evaluate run.
controls:
  # Governance + CI baseline (copied from github-level-2 as a starting point).
  - GOV-SEC-001
  - GOV-CON-002
  - GOV-COWN-003
  - GOV-LIC-004
  - CI-WF-005
  - CI-PERM-006
  - CI-DANGER-007
  - CI-PIN-008
  - CI-LEAST-009
  - SEC-CODEQL-010
  - SEC-DEPREV-011
  - REL-CHANGE-012
  - GOV-DISC-013
  - GOV-WAIV-014

  # SAST evidence layer.
  - SAST-SEMGREP-064
